WEBVTT

1
00:40:15.778 --> 00:40:24.778
Sit down, place your hand on your heart, close your eyes, focus on Jesus.

2
00:40:27.778 --> 00:40:35.778
Daddy is here, Jesus is here, Holy Spirit is here.

3
00:40:35.778 --> 00:40:43.778
They love you so deeply, you are so precious to them.

4
00:40:43.778 --> 00:40:51.778
They long for you, for intimacy with you, at this moment.

5
00:40:51.778 --> 00:40:57.778
No matter how things are, no matter what has happened.

6
00:40:57.778 --> 00:41:04.778
Whether you feel good or bad, whether you feel God very strongly at this moment.

7
00:41:04.778 --> 00:41:11.778
Or if you don't feel Him at all, it's not about feeling, He is here.

8
00:41:11.778 --> 00:41:16.778
The Bible is very clear about that, He is here.

9
00:41:16.778 --> 00:41:20.778
And He loves you, the Bible is very clear about that.

10
00:41:20.778 --> 00:41:24.778
You don't have to doubt if you don't feel it or anything like that.

11
00:41:24.778 --> 00:41:32.778
Or if you are struggling or don't understand things, He is here, in you, beside you.

12
00:41:32.778 --> 00:41:36.778
He wants to take you on His lap at this moment.

13
00:41:36.778 --> 00:41:42.778
Pressing you with His heart, hugging you.

14
00:41:42.778 --> 00:41:48.778
Wrapping His arm around you, as a protection, as a sealing.

15
00:41:53.778 --> 00:41:59.778
And in the spiritual world, He is the Lion of Judah who is roaring over you at this moment and crying out.

16
00:41:59.778 --> 00:42:06.778
Because He cannot stand how the adversary and the world are trying to tear you away.

17
00:42:06.778 --> 00:42:09.778
And trying to destroy the intimacy with Him.

18
00:42:11.778 --> 00:42:14.778
And He is more than a conqueror.

19
00:42:14.778 --> 00:42:16.778
And He sweeps everything aside.

20
00:42:16.778 --> 00:42:20.778
He roars and He sweeps it away.

21
00:42:20.778 --> 00:42:24.778
For you are my child and I love you.

22
00:42:24.778 --> 00:42:28.778
And everything that is turned against you, I am against.

23
00:42:28.778 --> 00:42:30.778
For you are mine.

24
00:42:30.778 --> 00:42:33.778
I have given my life for you.

25
00:42:33.778 --> 00:42:36.778
Because I love you dearly.

26
00:42:36.778 --> 00:42:39.778
Because I want to be intimate with you.

27
00:42:39.778 --> 00:42:42.778
Because I want to hug you, because I want to know you.

28
00:42:44.778 --> 00:42:48.778
Because I want to be your friend and experience your friendship.

29
00:42:48.778 --> 00:42:56.778
Because I long for your worship and your heart and your thoughts and your whole being that goes out to me.

30
00:42:59.778 --> 00:43:07.778
Just as we are completely intertwined in a trinity, I want to include you in that.

31
00:43:07.778 --> 00:43:10.778
And completely intertwine you with me.

32
00:43:10.778 --> 00:43:13.778
That we are one.

33
00:43:15.778 --> 00:43:20.778
I as God, you as my child, you all as my bride.

34
00:43:20.778 --> 00:43:23.778
I long for you.

35
00:43:23.778 --> 00:43:25.778
Let it all go.

36
00:43:25.778 --> 00:43:28.778
Surrender it all to me.

37
00:43:31.778 --> 00:43:36.778
Come Holy Spirit, touch everyone.

38
00:43:36.778 --> 00:43:39.778
Set us apart, press us to your heart.

39
00:43:39.778 --> 00:43:42.778
We long for you Lord, we need you Lord.

40
00:43:42.778 --> 00:43:46.778
We love you Lord, help us to love you more.

41
00:43:46.778 --> 00:43:50.778
We believe in you Lord, help us to believe more in you.

42
00:43:50.778 --> 00:43:54.778
We trust in you Lord, help us to trust more.

43
00:43:54.778 --> 00:43:57.778
Help us to trust more.

44
00:43:58.778 --> 00:44:03.778
We understand your heart, help us to understand you better.

45
00:44:04.778 --> 00:44:09.778
We are obedient to you, to your will and to your desires.

46
00:44:09.778 --> 00:44:12.778
Help us to be more obedient.

47
00:44:12.778 --> 00:44:14.778
Holding.

48
00:44:16.778 --> 00:44:18.778
God is good.

49
00:44:19.778 --> 00:44:23.778
I am sitting here for a moment because I feel a bit weak.

50
00:44:25.778 --> 00:44:28.778
But God is good, right, hallelujah.

51
00:44:28.778 --> 00:44:33.778
And at the same time we live in this world, in turbulent times.

52
00:44:35.778 --> 00:44:39.778
Wars, coups, banks that are on the verge of bankruptcy.

53
00:44:39.778 --> 00:44:43.778
Inflation, everything that is getting more expensive.

54
00:44:43.778 --> 00:44:45.778
We don't want that at all.

55
00:44:45.778 --> 00:44:50.778
We want a nice life, a good life, a secure life.

56
00:44:50.778 --> 00:44:52.778
Safety, stability.

57
00:44:54.778 --> 00:44:57.778
And we see so little of that around us.

58
00:44:57.778 --> 00:45:02.778
We live in the Western world and we are doing quite well there.

59
00:45:02.778 --> 00:45:05.778
If you compare it to other countries.

60
00:45:05.778 --> 00:45:07.778
We have a social system.

61
00:45:07.778 --> 00:45:11.778
If you are unemployed, you receive a benefit.

62
00:45:11.778 --> 00:45:15.778
If you are unemployed, you receive a benefit.

63
00:45:15.778 --> 00:45:17.778
You receive a pension.

64
00:45:19.778 --> 00:45:22.778
At the same time, all of that is also under pressure.

65
00:45:24.778 --> 00:45:30.778
In the past, you worked 50 years at Philips and then you had a good job.

66
00:45:30.778 --> 00:45:33.778
A stable salary and then you retired.

67
00:45:33.778 --> 00:45:35.778
And then you had a good pension.

68
00:45:35.778 --> 00:45:39.778
And then you could trust that your life was stable.

69
00:45:40.778 --> 00:45:45.778
That kind of thing is increasingly being eroded in our society.

70
00:45:45.778 --> 00:45:51.778
And then we are looking for security and safety in this world.

71
00:45:51.778 --> 00:45:55.778
Many people seek that in money.

72
00:45:56.778 --> 00:46:01.778
Making sure you have a good job or a good savings account.

73
00:46:01.778 --> 00:46:04.778
And saving well for your pension and so on.

74
00:46:04.778 --> 00:46:08.778
Building in as many things as possible to ensure you are safe.

75
00:46:08.778 --> 00:46:14.778
That you know that in a year, in five years, in ten years, in fifty years, it will still be safe for you.

76
00:46:14.778 --> 00:46:17.778
And in itself, those things are not wrong.

77
00:46:19.778 --> 00:46:22.778
And yet, there is something much better.

78
00:46:22.778 --> 00:46:25.778
Shall we take a look at Jeremiah 17?

79
00:46:31.778 --> 00:46:36.778
But if someone trusts in me, says God, I will take care of him.

80
00:46:36.778 --> 00:46:38.778
It will go well.

81
00:46:39.778 --> 00:46:42.778
He is like a tree planted by the water.

82
00:46:42.778 --> 00:46:45.778
Its roots grow to the stream.

83
00:46:45.778 --> 00:46:47.778
It doesn't even notice the heat.

84
00:46:47.778 --> 00:46:50.778
Its leaves always remain fresh and green.

85
00:46:50.778 --> 00:46:55.778
If there is a year without rain, it doesn't worry.

86
00:46:55.778 --> 00:46:59.778
There are always fruits growing on it.

87
00:47:01.778 --> 00:47:05.778
God says, if you trust in me, it will go well with you.

88
00:47:05.778 --> 00:47:07.778
That is what I was just talking about.

89
00:47:07.778 --> 00:47:10.778
Where do you find security in this world?

90
00:47:10.778 --> 00:47:14.778
Safety, stability, and certainty for the future.

91
00:47:14.778 --> 00:47:17.778
You find that with God, God promises here.

92
00:47:17.778 --> 00:47:21.778
If you trust in Him, He will ensure that it goes well with you.

93
00:47:21.778 --> 00:47:24.778
Where do you extend your roots?

94
00:47:24.778 --> 00:47:26.778
Do you extend your roots to God?

95
00:47:26.778 --> 00:47:31.778
As it says here in this verse, that your roots grow towards the stream.

96
00:47:31.778 --> 00:47:33.778
Grow in God's provision.

97
00:47:33.778 --> 00:47:37.778
Then comes the safety of your life and what will happen in the future.

98
00:47:37.778 --> 00:47:39.778
Whatever happens in this world.

99
00:47:39.778 --> 00:47:42.778
Whatever happens in your circumstances.

100
00:47:42.778 --> 00:47:45.778
Is God then your source?

101
00:47:45.778 --> 00:47:47.778
Are your roots planted in Him?

102
00:47:47.778 --> 00:47:52.778
So that even if it is a year of drought or everything goes wrong.

103
00:47:52.778 --> 00:47:56.778
You can still drink.

104
00:47:56.778 --> 00:48:02.778
Or are your roots planted in financial security?

105
00:48:02.778 --> 00:48:07.778
But that stream may dry up one day.

106
00:48:07.778 --> 00:48:13.778
We talked last week about the fruit of the Spirit.

107
00:48:13.778 --> 00:48:19.778
And the fruit of the Spirit is goodness.

108
00:48:19.778 --> 00:48:23.778
But also helpfulness.

109
00:48:23.778 --> 00:48:29.778
And also assistance, generosity.

110
00:48:29.778 --> 00:48:33.778
If your roots go deep in God.

111
00:48:33.778 --> 00:48:36.778
Then you just know that it will go well with you.

112
00:48:36.778 --> 00:48:40.778
Then you can be a blessing to the people around you.

113
00:48:40.778 --> 00:48:43.778
But if you build on your own financial security.

114
00:48:43.778 --> 00:48:47.778
Then it yields a different fruit.

115
00:48:48.778 --> 00:48:54.778
That brings uncertainty, doubts, worries, fear.

116
00:48:54.778 --> 00:48:58.778
Because then this happens again and then that happens again.

117
00:48:58.778 --> 00:49:02.778
Make sure you do it God's way.

118
00:49:02.778 --> 00:49:04.778
Put your roots down towards Him.

119
00:49:04.778 --> 00:49:06.778
Be generous.

120
00:49:06.778 --> 00:49:08.778
Trust in God, says God.

121
00:49:08.778 --> 00:49:09.778
How do you trust in God?

122
00:49:09.778 --> 00:49:13.778
Well, that is something you have to build up.

123
00:49:13.778 --> 00:49:17.778
You can't just flip a switch on that.

124
00:49:17.778 --> 00:49:19.778
In that, your relationship with God must grow.

125
00:49:19.778 --> 00:49:21.778
That's why you spend time with Him.

126
00:49:21.778 --> 00:49:25.778
Read the Bible, come to the services, come to the Monday evenings.

127
00:49:25.778 --> 00:49:27.778
Come to the lifegroups.

128
00:49:27.778 --> 00:49:30.778
And be engaged with God.

129
00:49:30.778 --> 00:49:33.778
But also do things in trust.

130
00:49:33.778 --> 00:49:40.778
Because trust does not grow if you don't do things that change something.

131
00:49:40.778 --> 00:49:42.778
If everything is just simple and easy.

132
00:49:42.778 --> 00:49:44.778
For example, with your giving.

133
00:49:44.778 --> 00:49:47.778
If you give a little money that you don't even notice.

134
00:49:47.778 --> 00:49:49.778
Then that trust doesn't grow there.

135
00:49:49.778 --> 00:49:52.778
But I have learned that if you dare to trust God.

136
00:49:52.778 --> 00:49:55.778
Also financially or perhaps especially financially.

137
00:49:55.778 --> 00:49:59.778
Then step by step you will notice that He is completely reliable.

138
00:49:59.778 --> 00:50:02.778
And that He loves you and wants to take care of you.

139
00:50:02.778 --> 00:50:12.778
Hello.

140
00:50:12.778 --> 00:50:15.778
Good morning everyone.

141
00:50:15.778 --> 00:50:18.778
Everyone happy?

142
00:50:18.778 --> 00:50:21.778
Three people.

143
00:50:21.778 --> 00:50:24.778
Then there is work to be done.

144
00:50:24.778 --> 00:50:26.778
Hallelujah.

145
00:50:26.778 --> 00:50:28.778
Shall we close our eyes?

146
00:50:28.778 --> 00:50:31.778
Maybe you want to stand for this prayer.

147
00:50:32.778 --> 00:50:38.778
Conversation.

148
00:50:38.778 --> 00:50:48.778
Holy Spirit, I want to ask you to bless the words that will be spoken here shortly.

149
00:50:48.778 --> 00:50:51.778
To bless them in the name of Jesus.

150
00:50:51.778 --> 00:50:58.778
And to bless that they will reach the hearts of the people.

151
00:50:58.778 --> 00:51:02.778
And I want to invite you, friend, in the audience.

152
00:51:02.778 --> 00:51:04.778
To open your heart.

153
00:51:04.778 --> 00:51:11.778
And to literally say, Holy Spirit, do your thing in my heart.

154
00:51:11.778 --> 00:51:15.778
Change me in those places where I need change.

155
00:51:15.778 --> 00:51:21.778
And affirm me in those things that you are pleased with.

156
00:51:21.778 --> 00:51:27.778
For the Holy Spirit can correct, but He is also a confirming God.

157
00:51:27.778 --> 00:51:30.778
For He is already present in you.

158
00:51:30.778 --> 00:51:32.778
Otherwise, you would not be here.

159
00:51:32.778 --> 00:51:34.778
He is already working with you.

160
00:51:34.778 --> 00:51:36.778
Otherwise, you would not be here.

161
00:51:36.778 --> 00:51:39.778
And I bless us all in the mighty name of Jesus.

162
00:51:39.778 --> 00:51:43.778
That the Word of God will come into us.

163
00:51:43.778 --> 00:51:47.778
And that it will bring about a change in our soul.

164
00:51:47.778 --> 00:51:49.778
In the name of Jesus.

165
00:51:49.778 --> 00:51:50.778
Amen.

166
00:51:50.778 --> 00:51:51.778
Amen.

167
00:51:51.778 --> 00:51:54.778
Please feel free to sit down.

168
00:51:55.778 --> 00:51:57.778
Yes, it is nice.

169
00:52:03.778 --> 00:52:14.778
We intentionally did not say during the MC to give each other a handshake or a hug or a blessing.

170
00:52:14.778 --> 00:52:20.778
Because at the end of this sermon, we will pray for each other.

171
00:52:20.778 --> 00:52:23.778
So the church will spring into action.

172
00:52:23.778 --> 00:52:25.778
I like that.

173
00:52:25.778 --> 00:52:27.778
Because as a church...

174
00:52:27.778 --> 00:52:29.778
Oh, that is nice.

175
00:52:29.778 --> 00:52:31.778
Don't you have it?

176
00:52:31.778 --> 00:52:33.778
Oh, that is nice.

177
00:52:33.778 --> 00:52:36.778
Ilias had turned it around a few days last week from the podium.

178
00:52:36.778 --> 00:52:38.778
Not during the service, or did he?

179
00:52:38.778 --> 00:52:40.778
That would be a classic.

180
00:52:40.778 --> 00:52:42.778
Delightful.

181
00:52:42.778 --> 00:52:46.778
But we are going to take action as a church shortly, if you all agree.

182
00:52:47.778 --> 00:52:51.778
So at the end of this sermon, we will pray for each other.

183
00:52:53.778 --> 00:52:57.778
Last week we talked about the fruits of the Spirit.

184
00:52:59.778 --> 00:53:13.778
Last week I indicated that the fruits of the Spirit are the result of what God does in us.

185
00:53:14.778 --> 00:53:18.778
And as we carry that out in faith.

186
00:53:18.778 --> 00:53:26.778
So what God does in us and how He has made us is one thing.

187
00:53:26.778 --> 00:53:28.778
The fruit is the result.

188
00:53:30.778 --> 00:53:34.778
Imagine you have a tree in your backyard.

189
00:53:34.778 --> 00:53:38.778
And it produces cherries.

190
00:53:38.778 --> 00:53:40.778
Delicious cherries.

191
00:53:41.778 --> 00:53:43.778
You take good care of that tree.

192
00:53:43.778 --> 00:53:45.778
You make sure it gets everything it needs.

193
00:53:45.778 --> 00:53:47.778
And you prune it.

194
00:53:47.778 --> 00:53:51.778
Then the result is that you get tasty cherries from it.

195
00:53:51.778 --> 00:53:57.778
Suppose that tree does not do that, then it may well be called a cherry tree.

196
00:53:57.778 --> 00:54:04.778
But if no delicious cherries come from it, you actually have very little of what that tree stands for.

197
00:54:04.778 --> 00:54:07.778
Maybe you could look at it and think that is a beautiful tree.

198
00:54:07.778 --> 00:54:11.778
But if you know it is a cherry tree but it produces nothing at all.

199
00:54:11.778 --> 00:54:14.778
Then you think to yourself, that is very unfortunate.

200
00:54:14.778 --> 00:54:25.778
So the fruits of the Spirit are, in my opinion, the most important results of who you are in God.

201
00:54:25.778 --> 00:54:26.778
Amen.

202
00:54:28.778 --> 00:54:29.778
Now.

203
00:54:29.778 --> 00:54:32.778
Today we are going to talk about the gifts of the Spirit.

204
00:54:32.778 --> 00:54:38.778
But let me first take a moment to reflect on the Holy Spirit Himself.

205
00:54:40.778 --> 00:54:43.778
Because when we talk about the Holy Spirit,

206
00:54:43.778 --> 00:54:51.778
you might think that the Holy Spirit came in the New Testament.

207
00:54:51.778 --> 00:54:58.778
And that He came during Pentecost, which we talked about a few weeks ago.

208
00:54:58.778 --> 00:55:04.778
So you have Easter, Ascension, and then Pentecost.

209
00:55:04.778 --> 00:55:09.778
During Easter in this church, we set up the large cross here.

210
00:55:09.778 --> 00:55:14.778
And we make it cozy and dress the theme of Easter.

211
00:55:14.778 --> 00:55:21.778
Because we believe that Easter is the most important celebration that a Christian can celebrate.

212
00:55:21.778 --> 00:55:24.778
Not Christmas, but Easter.

213
00:55:24.778 --> 00:55:32.778
Easter is indeed the celebration that Jesus Himself said to keep celebrating.

214
00:55:32.778 --> 00:55:36.778
Jesus never commanded us to celebrate Christmas.

215
00:55:36.778 --> 00:55:39.778
That is a creation of the church itself.

216
00:55:39.778 --> 00:55:42.778
And that is not wrong; it is not sinful.

217
00:55:42.778 --> 00:55:45.778
It is just not a command from Jesus.

218
00:55:46.778 --> 00:55:50.778
You see this often; Paul also says something in one of his letters.

219
00:55:50.778 --> 00:55:54.778
And he says, this is my own advice.

220
00:55:54.778 --> 00:55:57.778
Not advice personally from the Lord Himself.

221
00:55:57.778 --> 00:56:00.778
So something that the church itself invents is not necessarily wrong.

222
00:56:00.778 --> 00:56:05.778
If we organize a barbecue, that is not sinful, but that is obviously delightful.

223
00:56:05.778 --> 00:56:12.778
But Easter is literally what Jesus commands us to celebrate.

224
00:56:12.778 --> 00:56:15.778
And here is the sequence, here is the order.

225
00:56:15.778 --> 00:56:21.778
First you have Easter, because Easter is the most, most important thing of our faith.

226
00:56:21.778 --> 00:56:29.778
For God loves the world so much that He has given His one and only Son to us.

227
00:56:29.778 --> 00:56:35.778
So that everyone who believes in Him shall not perish but have eternal life.

228
00:56:35.778 --> 00:56:37.778
And I can say amen to that.

229
00:56:37.778 --> 00:56:40.778
That's it, that is our faith.

230
00:56:40.778 --> 00:56:45.778
Imagine you are walking down the street and you just know by God's Spirit,

231
00:56:45.778 --> 00:56:50.778
that the moment has come for you to speak to someone about the love of God.

232
00:56:50.778 --> 00:56:53.778
John 3 verse 16, can't miss with that one.

233
00:56:53.778 --> 00:56:57.778
It is simply the best, sharpest Bible verse there is.

234
00:56:57.778 --> 00:57:03.778
God loves you and He has given Jesus so that you can believe in Jesus.

235
00:57:03.778 --> 00:57:06.778
For if you believe in Jesus, you are no longer lost.

236
00:57:06.778 --> 00:57:09.778
Not in this world and not in the world to come.

237
00:57:09.778 --> 00:57:13.778
Never lost again by the mighty name of Jesus.

238
00:57:13.778 --> 00:57:16.778
Glory to Him, hallelujah.

239
00:57:16.778 --> 00:57:18.778
And then we have the ascension.

240
00:57:18.778 --> 00:57:22.778
Jesus comes together with His disciples on a mountain.

241
00:57:22.778 --> 00:57:24.778
Nice thematic, on a mountain.

242
00:57:24.778 --> 00:57:27.778
And from the mountain, He goes back to heaven.

243
00:57:27.778 --> 00:57:30.778
So Easter, ascension.

244
00:57:30.778 --> 00:57:36.778
And in the commission of Jesus, the disciples go to the upper room in Jerusalem.

245
00:57:36.778 --> 00:57:40.778
And there they receive the Holy Spirit.

246
00:57:40.778 --> 00:57:46.778
And so, as Christians, we sometimes think that the Holy Spirit came in the New Testament.

247
00:57:46.778 --> 00:57:50.778
We sometimes think that the Holy Spirit only came then.

248
00:57:50.778 --> 00:57:55.778
As if He kept Himself behind the scenes before that time.

249
00:57:55.778 --> 00:58:01.778
But let me inform you that the Holy Spirit has always been there.

250
00:58:01.778 --> 00:58:05.778
The Holy Spirit is the Spirit of God.

